WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.925
Here's Microsoft's starting point.

2
00:00:01.925 --> 00:00:07.020
Microsoft's Zero Trust recommendations
for both services check prevention mode,

3
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.590
request body inspection, the default
rule set, the bot protection rule set,

4
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:14.812
rate limiting and diagnostic
logging, among others.

5
00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:19.755
Learn recommends the latest Default Rule
Set, two point two at the guide's reading,

6
00:00:19.755 --> 00:00:24.699
validated in log mode before blocking; the
command line's default is two point one.

7
00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:27.488
Front Door's managed rules
need the Premium tier.

8
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:32.176
Built-in policies require a WAF on
each service, and a given mode.

9
00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:37.010
And Learn documents the switch between
detection and prevention with one command.
